==Description== <!--T:3-->

<!--T:4-->
The SuppressedIndices property allows you to selectively suppress (skip) specific occurrences in a pattern feature.

</translate>
[[File:PartDesign_SuppressedIndices_example.png|200px]]
<translate>

==Usage== <!--T:5-->

<!--T:6-->
# Create a pattern feature (e.g., Linear Pattern or Polar Pattern).
# Double-click the pattern feature in the Tree View to open its task panel.
# In the task panel, find the Suppressed Indices property.
# Enter the indices of the occurrences you want to suppress, separated by commas.
# Click OK.

==Options== <!--T:7-->

<!--T:8-->
* The indices are 0-based: the first occurrence has index 0, the second has index 1, etc.
* You can suppress multiple occurrences by entering comma-separated indices.
* Suppressed occurrences are not created and do not appear in the Tree View.

==Properties== <!--T:9-->

<!--T:10-->
* SuppressedIndices: a list of indices to suppress in the pattern.

</translate>
